vms-f97: alpha-dec-vms — derive the "..en" procedure entry label from the
resolved (transparent-alias-decorated) name, matching .ent/.pdesc.

Operator-ruled (vms-f97) minimal codegen-consistency fix for the alpha-dec-vms
GCC 14.2.0 port. When cc1 compiles a *definition* of a recognized OpenVMS C-RTL
name (e.g. musl's strlen/malloc/memcpy/vsnprintf), the port's transparent alias
(vms_patch_builtins / IDENTIFIER_TRANSPARENT_ALIAS, gcc/config/vms/vms.cc)
redirects the name to its "decc$"-prefixed variant. assemble_name() applies that
alias when it emits ".ent decc$strlen" and ".pdesc decc$strlen..en", but
alpha_start_function built the entry label by appending "..en" to the RAW base
name and emitting it through ASM_OUTPUT_FUNCTION_LABEL. assemble_name() cannot
resolve the combined string "strlen..en" to an identifier, so the label came out
as "strlen..en" while .pdesc referenced "decc$strlen..en" — a label that does
not exist. GAS then rejects the object (~52% of musl: all decc$-recognized RTL
definitions).

Fix: resolve fnname via assemble_name_resolve() (the exact routine assemble_name
uses) BEFORE appending "..en", so the entry label is "decc$strlen..en" for a
recognized C-RTL name and unchanged ("myfunc..en") for every other name (base ==
decorated). Guarded on TARGET_ABI_OPEN_VMS; the OSF path is untouched. The
alloca sizing is widened to the resolved name so the longer "decc$" form fits.

This is an internal-consistency fix only (entry label must match .ent/.pdesc);
it does not change the decoration behavior itself. Sanctioned by the operator
ruling to "make the port build" (path A to the Alpha DECC$SHR).

Clean-room (Rule 8): derived from public GCC source structure + observed cc1
assembly output only; no VSI/HPE source consulted.

--- a/gcc/config/alpha/alpha.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/alpha/alpha.cc
@@ -8008,7 +8008,18 @@
   const HOST_WIDE_INT max_frame_size = HOST_WIDE_INT_1 << 31;
   /* Offset from base reg to register save area.  */
   HOST_WIDE_INT reg_offset;
-  char *entry_label = (char *) alloca (strlen (fnname) + 6);
+  /* vms-f97 (OVMX): the procedure entry label ("..en") must be derived
+     from the SAME resolved name that .ent and .pdesc use.  On the
+     OpenVMS ABI a recognized C-RTL name is redirected to its
+     "decc$"-prefixed variant via IDENTIFIER_TRANSPARENT_ALIAS
+     (config/vms/vms.cc); assemble_name () applies that alias when it
+     emits .ent/.pdesc, but appending "..en" to the raw base name
+     before output defeats the alias lookup, so the label came out as
+     `strlen..en` while .pdesc referenced `decc$strlen..en` -> GAS
+     rejects the missing label.  Resolve first, then append "..en".  */
+  const char *resolved_fnname
+    = TARGET_ABI_OPEN_VMS ? assemble_name_resolve (fnname) : fnname;
+  char *entry_label = (char *) alloca (strlen (resolved_fnname) + 6);
   char *tramp_label = (char *) alloca (strlen (fnname) + 6);
   int i;
 
@@ -8060,7 +8071,7 @@
 	fprintf (file, "\tldq $27,16($27)\n");
      }
 
-  strcpy (entry_label, fnname);
+  strcpy (entry_label, resolved_fnname);
   if (TARGET_ABI_OPEN_VMS)
     strcat (entry_label, "..en");
 
